1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,393
Welcome to the AI Academic Advisor of Vidyashilp University.

2
00:00:05,393 --> 00:00:10,940
An advisor that knows when to answer, what to answer, when to ask,

3
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:13,630
and when to say it doesn't know.

4
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:16,911
A student's question sounds simple.

5
00:00:16,911 --> 00:00:19,769
Can I take Machine Learning next semester?

6
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:24,735
But the answer depends on the handbook, the semester spread, their batch,

7
00:00:24,735 --> 00:00:26,164
and their own record.

8
00:00:26,164 --> 00:00:28,410
A general chatbot simply guesses.

9
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:33,193
So every answer starts from the university's own documents.

10
00:00:33,193 --> 00:00:35,562
Each question passes a safety check.

11
00:00:35,562 --> 00:00:38,788
Exact questions go straight to a course database.

12
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:43,066
Everything else uses retrieval from the handbook, the procedures,

13
00:00:43,066 --> 00:00:46,950
and the course lists, and the model must cite what it uses.

14
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:49,311
Take this question.

15
00:00:49,311 --> 00:00:53,235
How many courses are in the 2022 Foundation basket?

16
00:00:53,235 --> 00:00:58,159
The advisor returns fourteen courses, worth thirty-four credits,

17
00:00:58,159 --> 00:00:59,698
with the full table.

18
00:00:59,698 --> 00:01:04,930
No model was needed, so it used zero tokens, and it cannot miscount.

19
00:01:05,829 --> 00:01:08,322
When information is missing, it asks.

20
00:01:08,322 --> 00:01:09,872
Which batch are you in?

21
00:01:09,872 --> 00:01:12,297
Which prerequisites have you passed?

22
00:01:12,297 --> 00:01:16,002
When the documents don't contain an answer, it says so,

23
00:01:16,002 --> 00:01:19,909
and names the office to contact, instead of making one up.

24
00:01:20,809 --> 00:01:24,596
For eligibility, the work is split across six steps.

25
00:01:24,596 --> 00:01:26,708
A planner reads the question.

26
00:01:26,708 --> 00:01:28,602
Retrieval finds the rules.

27
00:01:28,602 --> 00:01:33,190
Eligibility and credits are worked out in code, not by a model.

28
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:35,229
A recommendation is written,

29
00:01:35,229 --> 00:01:39,889
and verification checks every number before the student sees it.

30
00:01:40,789 --> 00:01:44,973
Students can ask by voice, and check the words before sending.

31
00:01:44,973 --> 00:01:47,739
They can upload a photo of a grade sheet,

32
00:01:47,739 --> 00:01:50,505
and confirm every grade before it's used.

33
00:01:50,505 --> 00:01:52,462
They can listen to an answer,

34
00:01:52,462 --> 00:01:57,590
or see their whole programme as an infographic drawn directly from the data.

35
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:03,191
We attacked it, too, with twenty-six prompt injections and privacy attempts.

36
00:02:03,191 --> 00:02:07,583
With the safety layer, none succeeded, and only four reached the model.

37
00:02:07,583 --> 00:02:11,295
Phone numbers and I D numbers are removed before processing,

38
00:02:11,295 --> 00:02:13,769
and another student's record is refused.

39
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,444
And people stay in charge.

40
00:02:16,444 --> 00:02:20,199
The advisor can't change a record or approve a request.

41
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:24,636
For appeals, medical cases, and graduation, it explains the rule,

42
00:02:24,636 --> 00:02:26,070
and says who decides.

43
00:02:26,970 --> 00:02:28,690
Grounded in documents.

44
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,568
Honest about its limits.

45
00:02:30,568 --> 00:02:33,149
And designed to work with people.

46
00:02:33,149 --> 00:02:35,652
This is the AI Academic Advisor.

47
00:02:35,652 --> 00:02:37,529
Try the live demo today.
